          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong monoidal adjunction
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
            which respects the monoidal structure.
          %p
            Since there are several types of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+functors"} monoidal functors
            (lax, colax, and strong) there are several types of “adjunctions between monoidal categories which respect the monoidal structure.” Namely, we could have:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                An adjunction in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MonCat"} MonCat
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functors"} strong monoidal functors
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %munderover
                                %mrow
                                %munder
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi R
                                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                    %mtext strong monoidal
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟵
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi L
                                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                    %mtext strong monoidal
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \\underoverset
                      {\underset{R \, \text{strong monoidal}}{\longrightarrow}}
                      {\overset{L \, \text{strong monoidal}}{\longleftarrow}}
                      {}
                      }
              %p
                We call this a
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong strong monoidal adjunction
            %li#MonoidalAdjnctionIdea
              %p
                An adjunction in the 2-category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MonCat"} MonCat
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mrow
                        %mi ℓ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_\ell
                of monoidal categories and
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functors"} lax monoidal functors
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/doctrinal+adjunction"} doctrinal adjunction
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/show/doctrinal+adjunction#strength"} here
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %munderover
                                %mrow
                                %munder
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi R
                                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                    %mtext lax monoidal
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟵
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi L
                                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                    %mtext strong monoidal
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \\underoverset
                      {\underset{R \, \text{lax monoidal}}{\longrightarrow}}
                      {\overset{L \, \text{strong monoidal}}{\longleftarrow}}
                      {}
                      }
              %p
                In fact, since the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
                of an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oplax+monoidal+functor"} oplax monoidal functor
                is necessarily a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal functor
                (
                %a{:href => "oplax+monoidal+functor#OplaxAdjointToLax"}> this prop.
                ), it is sufficient to demand that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                be strong monoidal.
              %p
                This version, which is one of the most frequently occurring, is often called simply a
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong monoidal adjunction
            %li
              %p
                The dual: an adjunction in the 2-category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi MonCat
                        %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MonCat_c
                of monoidal categories and colax monoidal functors, in which case the left adjoint is colax and the right adjoint is strong. One might call this an
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong opmonoidal adjunction
            %li
              %p
                A mixed situation, in which the left adjoint is colax, the right adjoint is lax, and the lax and colax structure maps are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mates"} mates
                under the adjunction. This is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjunction"} conjunction
                in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+category"} double category
                of monoidal categories and lax and colax monoidal functors, so we may call it a
                %strong monoidal conjunction
                or a
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong lax/colax monoidal adjunction
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/doctrinal+adjunction"} doctrinal adjunction
          %h2#Details Details
          %p
            As mentioned
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MonoidalAdjnctionIdea"} above
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/doctrinal+adjunctions"} doctrinal adjunctions
          #MonoidalAdjunctionElementary.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
