                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi μ
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta(A) \circ \mu_A
            %p Finally we need to check that the following diagram commutes:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi e
                                    %mi A
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi e
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi R
                                      %mi L
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                      %mi A
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi η
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi A
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; 1
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{e_A}}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{ e_{R L (A)} }}
                    \\\
                    A
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\underset{\eta(A)}{\longrightarrow}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    R L(A)
                    }
            %p
              Now unwinding the above definitions of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_{R L}(A)
              in terms of the definition of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_R
              we find that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi η
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi R
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi e
                          %mi L
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi R
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi R
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    e_{R L (A)}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    1
                    \\overset{\eta(1)}{\longrightarrow}
                    R L(1)
                    \\overset{R(e_L^{-1})}{\longrightarrow}
                    R(1)
                    \\overset{R(e_L)}{\longrightarrow} R L(1) \overset{R L(e_a)}{\longrightarrow} R L(A)
                    \\,.
            %p Here the two morphisms in the middle cancel, so that we are left just with
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi η
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi R
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi R
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    e_{R L(A)}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    1
                    \\overset{\eta(1)}{\longrightarrow}
                    R L(1)
                    \\overset{R L(e_A)}{\longrightarrow}
                    R L (A)
                    \\,.
            %p
              That this equals
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta(A)\circ e_A
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi η
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi e
                                    %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi R
                                  %mi L
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi e
                                    %mi A
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi η
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi A
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    1
                    \&amp;\overset{\eta(1)}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    R L(1)
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{e_A}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{R L(e_A)}}
                    \\\
                    A &amp;\underset{\eta(A)}{\longrightarrow}&amp; R L(A)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p The argument for the homomorphism property of the counit should be formally dual to the above.
          %h2#examples Examples
          #Stabilization.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
                in
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
              adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spectra
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mn ∞
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Σ
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Spaces
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo +
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spaces
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Ho(Spectra)
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{\Omega^\infty}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{\Sigma^\infty(-)}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    Ho(Spaces^{\ast/})
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{(-)_+}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {}
                    Ho(Spaces)
            %p
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+homotopy+categories"} classical homotopy categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spaces
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Spaces)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Spaces
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Spaces^{\ast/})
              of (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+space"}> pointed
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spectra
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Spectra)
              is a monoidal adjunction, since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^\infty(-)_+
              (forming the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectrum"} suspension spectrum
              of a space after freely
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+space"} adjoining a basepoint
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal
              with respect to forming
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+spaces"} product topological spaces
              and forming
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product+of+spectra"} smash product of spectra
            %p
              In fact this is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functors"} derived functors
              of what is even a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+Quillen+adjunction"} monoidal Quillen adjunction
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
              and the stable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+orthogonal+spectra"} model structure on orthogonal spectra
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-2#StableMonoidalQuillenSuspensionSpectrumFunctor"}> this cor.
              ), which implies (strong) monoidality of the derived functors on homotopy categories (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-2#StrongMonoidalDerivedFunctorFromStrongMonoidalQuillenAdjunction"}> this prop.
              ).
            %p In detail, let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi orth
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi stable
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi orth
                            %mn ∞
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi orth
                            %mn ∞
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi Quillen
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi Quillen
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (L \dashv R)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\mathbb{S}_{orth}Mod_{stable}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{\Omega^\infty_{orth}}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{\Sigma^\infty_{orth}}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    Top^{\ast/}_{Quillen}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{(-)_+}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    Top_{Quillen}
            %p
              be the Quillen adjunction on orthogonal spectra (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-2#SuspensionSpectrumStructuredStrictQuillenAdjunction"}> here
              ). The left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              is a strong monoidal functor, and hence so is its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spectra
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^\infty(-)_+ \colon Ho(Top) \to Ho(Spectra)
              (by
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-2#StrongMonoidalDerivedFunctorFromStrongMonoidalQuillenAdjunction"} this prop.
            %p#DerivedLaxMonoidalStructure
              We want to see that the structure of a lax monoidal functor which is induced on the derived right adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spectra
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\infty(-) \colon Ho(Top) \to Ho(Spectra)
              via prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalAdjunctionElementary"}
              is the expected one, given on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Omega-spectra"} Omega-spectra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mn 0
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi Y
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega^\infty(X) \wedge \Omega^\infty(X)
                    \=
                    X_0 \wedge Y_0
                    \\overset{}{\to}
                    (X \wedge Y)_0
                    \=
                    \\Omega^\infty( X \wedge Y )
                    \\,.
            %p
              To see this, observe that if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-spectrum"} CW-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Omega-spectra"} Omega-spectra
              and hence cofibrant and fibrant in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi orth
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi stable
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{orth}Mod_{stable}
              then the derived lax monoidal structure is given by the total bottom composite in the following diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi R
